{"id":"CVE-2020-28366","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2020-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T16:33:58.955Z","title":"Arbitrary code execution in go command with cgo in cmd/go and cmd/cgo","description":"Code injection in the go command with cgo before Go 1.14.12 and Go 1.15.5 allows arbitrary code execution at build time via a malicious unquoted symbol name in a linked object file.","cwe":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Go toolchain","product":"cmd/go","packageName":"cmd/go","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.14.12 (semver)","affected 1.15.0-0 <1.15.5 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"Go toolchain","product":"cmd/cgo","packageName":"cmd/cgo","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.14.12 (semver)","affected 1.15.0-0 <1.15.5 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://go.dev/cl/269658"},{"url":"https://go.googlesource.com/go/+/062e0e5ce6df339dc26732438ad771f73dbf2292"},{"url":"https://go.dev/issue/42559"},{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/NpBGTTmKzpM"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2022-0475"}],"credits":["Chris Brown (Tempus Ex)"],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-28367","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2020-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-04T16:33:59.087Z","title":"Arbitrary code execution via the go command with cgo in cmd/go","description":"Code injection in the go command with cgo before Go 1.14.12 and Go 1.15.5 allows arbitrary code execution at build time via malicious gcc flags specified via a #cgo directive.","cwe":["CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Go toolchain","product":"cmd/go","packageName":"cmd/go","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.14.12 (semver)","affected 1.15.0-0 <1.15.5 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://go.dev/cl/267277"},{"url":"https://go.googlesource.com/go/+/da7aa86917811a571e6634b45a457f918b8e6561"},{"url":"https://go.dev/issue/42556"},{"url":"https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/NpBGTTmKzpM"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2022-0476"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/04/msg00021.html"}],"credits":["Imre Rad"],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2020-29509","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Mattermost","published":"2020-12-14T20:02:02.448Z","updated":"2024-09-17T03:43:39.703Z","description":"The encoding/xml package in Go (all versions) does not correctly preserve the semantics of attribute namespace prefixes during tokenization round-trips, which allows an attacker to craft inputs that behave in conflicting ways during different stages of processing in affected downstream applications.","cwe":["CWE-115 CWE-115 Misinterpretation of Input"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Golang","product":"Go","versions":["affected All versions"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/mattermost/xml-roundtrip-validator/blob/master/advisories/unstable-attributes.md","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20210129-0006/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"workarounds":["Untrusted markup in affected applications can be validated using the github.com/mattermost/xml-roundtrip-validator module."],"vendors":["golang"]}
